          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em linear isometry
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi
                  \\,\colon\,
                  \\mathscr{H}_1
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathscr{H}_2
          %p
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+space"} normed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            which preserves the norm:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ‖
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ‖
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ‖
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ‖
                    %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\big\Vert \psi(-) \big\Vert_2
                  \\;=\;
                  \\big\Vert - \big\Vert_1
                  \\,.
          %p
            In particular, when the norm is induced by (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+form"}> Hermitian
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+products"} inner products
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\langle \cdot \vert \cdot \rangle}_{i}
            (as on
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+spaces"} Hilbert spaces
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ‖
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ‖
                    %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ≡
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msqrt
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mrow
                          %mo ⟨
                          %mi ψ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi ψ
                          %mo ⟩
                        %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  {\big\Vert \psi \big\Vert}_i
                  \\,\equiv\,
                  \\sqrt{
                  \\left\langle \psi \vert \psi \right\rangle_i
                  }
          %p
            then a linear isometry is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isometry"} isometry
            in that it preserves these inner products:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⟨
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo −
                      %mo ⟩
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\big\langle \phi(-) \vert \phi(-) \big\rangle_2
                  \\;=\;
                  \\left\langle - \vert - \right\rangle_1
          %p
            or equivalently, in terms of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+operators"} adjoint operators
          #eq:InTermsOfAdjointOperators.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo †
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Id
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi.mathscript ℋ
                        %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi^\dagger \cdot \phi \,=\, Id_{\mathscr{H}_1}
                  \\,.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (relation to unitary operators)
              %br/
              If in addition to
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:InTermsOfAdjointOperators"} (1)
              also the reverse condition
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo †
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \cdot \phi^\dagger \,=\, Id_{\mathscr{H}_2}
              holds, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              is called a
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+operator"} unitary operator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjective+map"} surjective map
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
          #LinearIsometriesAreInjective.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Linear isometries are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+maps"} injective maps
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo ⟩
                    %mo ,
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ⟩
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left\vert \psi \right\rangle, \left\vert \psi' \right\rangle \,\colon\, \mathscr{H}
              we need to show that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo ⟩
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ⟩
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo ⟩
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ⟩
                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi\left\vert \psi \right\rangle
                    \\;=\;
                    \\phi\left\vert \psi' \right\rangle
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    \\Rightarrow
                    \\;\;\;\;
                    \\left\vert \psi \right\rangle
                    \\;=\;
                    \\left\vert \psi' \right\rangle
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
            %p But by non-degeneracy of the norm this is equivalent to showing
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ‖
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %mrow
                        %mo |
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo ⟩
                      %mo −
                      %mrow
                        %mo |
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ⟩
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ‖
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ‖
                      %mrow
                        %mo |
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo ⟩
                      %mo −
                      %mrow
                        %mo |
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ⟩
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ‖
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mn 0
                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {
                    \\Big\Vert
                    \\phi
                    \\big(
                    \\left\vert \psi \right\rangle
                    \-
                    \\left\vert \psi' \right\rangle
                    \\big)
                    \\Big\Vert
                    }
                    \\,=\,
                    0
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\Rightarrow
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    {
                    \\Big\Vert
                    \\left\vert \psi \right\rangle
                    \-
                    \\left\vert \psi' \right\rangle
                    \\Big\Vert
                    }
                    \\,=\,
                    0
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
            %p
              But since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              is an isometry, here the left hand side already coincides with the right hand side and hence certainly implies it.
